{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1012775-paradoxical-sidereal-thoughts","id":1012775,"title":"Paradoxical Sidereal Thoughts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-05T14:24:46-08:00","id":1012775,"title":"Paradoxical Sidereal Thoughts","content":"I've been one of the stubborn ones when it comes to Sidereals for a long time, and have always argued for them to stay the same. Don't mess with Astrology, don't let them create Charms, and so on. Because most of us don't want to lose the 'magic' of 1e Sidereals.<br /> <br /> So it's ironic that I'm the one suggesting this.<br /> <br /> But since 3e is a time of new beginnings, maybe it's time to get rid of Paradox completely. Pattern Spider Bite was a fun mechanic, but it's primary reason for existing was because Sidereals didn't have a standard Limit flaw, and having two is just too much when one of them acts as a hindrance to Astrology. One of the things about 3e is getting rid of such hindrances and speed bumps that might keep you from doing the 'cool stuff', which is why Excellencies are free now and Solars start with more than 10 Charms. Some of the effects and triggers of Paradox could be retained and folded into the Sidereal Limit flaw without too much trouble I think, and Sidereal players would no longer feel punished for using Astrology. While Censure provides a method of reigning in excesses that's more appropriate from a setting perspective as it is more of a roleplaying instrument rather than a strict mechanical one. Whatever other changes to Astrology that might (or might not) come, I think that's one that should definitely be made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12167-broken-masque","name":"Broken Masque","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T14:57:42-08:00","id":1012800,"title":"","content":"The Sidereal limiters did not age well, and while I won't question them working in 1E (never actually played that edition) in 2E they were flat out antagonistic to players. So much so most players I run into say &quot;fuck even learning astrology&quot;. After being in a game with no paradox (for the most part, big reality rending stuff still caused it) and colleges=abilities I don't think I could ever go back. Only being able to make M.A. charms and spells seriously hurts charm diversity, you have four favored slots and every Character has to favor occult/M.A. or your hurting the character in a long term game. Nobody else deals with that bullshit and shouldn't have to. Sidereals have plenty of hoops to jump through for esoteric gameplay that rewards the clever/dedicated without pointlessly punishing them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T15:13:41-08:00","id":1012804,"title":"","content":"I think Paradox makes a good non-standard charm cost. Instead of a charm that can only be activated once per-scene unless you reset it, you can have something that you can use as many times as you like but getting more than 10 points is bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T15:24:02-08:00","id":1012815,"title":"","content":"I <i>loathe</i> pattern bite. &quot;You dare use your basic power? Take 7 aggravated.&quot; is such a fucking terrible mechanic. It's not evocative, it's not interesting, it's just &quot;Tear up your character sheet. That'll teach you to play the game.&quot;<br /> <br /> Closed charmsets, though, I like, because I like the idea that &quot;The maidens saw into the future and created every Charm Sidereals would ever really need&quot;.<br /> Players (and I'm including the ST because the ST is a player) should never forget that they aren't the Sidereals. Nothing stops us from declaring a homebrewed charm to have always existed in-universe. (&quot;Why don't the other Sidereals know it&quot;, you ask? Maybe they do and none of the PCs have ever seen it in action. Or maybe the Maiden of Secrets kept it hidden all this time. etc. etc. handwave handwave)<br /> <br /> There are ways of making paradox interesting, of course, but the current implimentation isn't it, imo. I wrote up a prototype of what I'd have liked to see somewhere. I'll see if I can find it again.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: here it is. If you notice the peculiar terminology, it's because it's from a sidereal homebrew thread, but it doesn't really affect the overall idea.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/591474-kickstarter-update-79?p=602357#post602357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Tell me about it</i>. In Awakening, a horror game where reality is literally out to punish you and erase you from existence, Paradox <i>still</i> isn't as bad (read: is more fun) as it is in a game about high-octane kung-fu bureaucrats. <i>Come the fuck on!</i><br /> <br /> I like the vision that it's bureaucratic red tape and that you can lower it by staying late at work, but it's still missing an actual engagement mechanic. Doing generic extra paperwork isn't engaging, nor is trying to weasel into the smallest possible paradox pool (it might be intellectually rewarding the first couple of times, but once you've solved that puzzle it's just rote).<br /> <br /> By &quot;engagement mechanic&quot;, I mean something that actually generates story and player action. Examples include:<ul><li> Your Fate Request means that the pattern spiders can't overlook a certain aspect of creation, causing reality glitches that you must fix.</li> <li> Your Fate Request directly competes with an other one, creating a destiny loophole that the PS are too busy to solve. Solve it yourself or get the other party to cancel their request.</li> <li> The Pattern Spiders are tired of your bullshit and have decided to give you the silent treatment. You are now a glitch. Every Scene that you start in Creation, roll a d10. On a 1, you cease to interact with Creation, as though you were an illusion, until you pay a cost equivalent to what gods pay to Materialize. On a 7, you are mistaken for a local celebrity by literally everyone. On a 10, you gain [essence] points of storyteller-decided mutations for the remainder of the session. These points stack, but are purely cosmetic and don't actually exist, they just look like they do.</li> <li> The Pattern Spiders are <i>so</i> tired of your bullshit that they're taking it out on you. Gain the Enemy flaw for the remainder of the story at a level deemed appropriate by teh ST. This may be a scorned lover, an ally who feels betrayed or a Deathlord that decided that you are their next plaything.</li> <li> Seriously, stop pissing off the pattern spiders, they gave your address to some fairfolk/demons/ghosts that were looking for a good time, and more will come until you do X.</li> <li> I warned you about the pattern spiders, bro. I warned you dawg: Instead of giving you the silent treatment, they're giving you an angry rant. Sometimes stairs lead to the opposite of their destination, doors open to the wrong room, even your own pockets are sometimes those of someone else. Whenever you roll for an action, roll a d10. If the resulting face is higher than your amount of successes on that action, the environment changes such that the opposite happens. For unrolled actions, treat this number as 5. This doesn't apply to combat. They're mad, but they're not <i>that</i> mad. Yet.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/852992-brainstorming-sidereals-and-the-great-curse?p=859666#post859666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I gotta agree with Unsung Hero. Just suffering damage is one of the effects of Pattern Bite that was the least interesting, same for catatonia. It's not really fun to just be taken out of the game.<br /> <br /> Something that creates plot hooks or gets players to act in interesting ways usually works better.<br /> <br /> Some suggestions for madnesses:<ul><li> The characters intimacies are reversed for a [day/week?], and the player must act accordingly.</li> <li> The sidereal gains a fixation they must adhere to, like speaking only in rhymes or needing to mention the subject of their kismet in every sentence (and rolling a die of paradox if they fail to do so).</li> <li> Once per scene for one session, the Sidereal gets either nightmarish or ecstatic, but very vivid and potent, hallucinations relating to their kismet, which the Sidereal is convinced are prophetic (but may not be).</li> <li> For a day/week the Sidereal dissociates from their identity, becoming convinced that they are someone else entirely, often using Resplendent Destinies to this effect. Attempting to reconcile them with their &quot;true&quot; self causes distress and tangles their fate further, either draining one WP or adding a die of Paradox. Repeated attempts may trigger the Sidereal to withdraw further into their new personality as the paradox reactivates. Once the effect passes, they remember both selves as being simultaneously true.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 12-05-2016, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T16:14:11-08:00","id":1012855,"title":"","content":"I don't mind the idea of Paradox as an additional cost to certain Charms. Some stronger Charms might cost Essence, Willpower and give you Paradox. When you hit maximum Paradox something bad happens - though obviously not on the level of, &quot;You die&quot; or &quot;you fall into a coma for a month&quot; or anything like that. But I think that the basic concept of Paradox can be salvaged and made interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T16:30:42-08:00","id":1012859,"title":"","content":"To diverge very briefly on the subject of the Sidereal closed Charmset, I think the splat will benefit greatly from both the charm mechanics that were created after the 2e Sidereal book, but by now are well established. Namely Charms that gain new powers when the Exalt reaches a certain Essence level, or when you have the option to re-buy a Charm for expanded powers. The true problem with the closed Charmset is that the simple limits of practicality mean they can only devote so much space in the book to Charms, and so must choose the Charms that are 'best' for them overall, whether or not there are others that would also fit and be very useful for Sidereals (and I for one have also been of the mind that ST's and Players can get together and decide that &quot;this custom Charm has <i>always</i> existed&quot; when it suits). At the very least the previously mentioned mechanics can save on word count so they can get more of those Charms in. And that's all I'll really say about that, before I side-track my own thread completely.<br /> <br /> I certainly wouldn't mind going back to Paradox as the a mechanical flaw, but obviously with more interesting traits to it than like those mentioned. I never felt really comfortable with the Sidereal Limit mechanic from a storytelling standpoint even more than the mechanical in 2e, even if the purely roleplayed Limit flaw was easy to miss, and sometimes hard to pull off in 1e. And using Paradox as a cost for high-level Charms and large abuses of Astrology would make a lot more sense than Limit ever would. Perhaps even Astrological ones, who knows honestly... I'm more open to change overall this time around, though I think the core of what makes Sidereals what they are should be retained from past editions. And I also just considered that since we have multiple new types of Exalts, including some that were never around to be cursed by the Neverborn, it's logical to propose that a Limit track will not be universal either, though I think we can count on there being something similar for everyone.<br /> <br /> And Fata-Ku... I love the ideas you have there for Paradox, but won't be able to give a full commentary of them until I'm able to stop chuckling. But I will say it's exactly the kind of weird shit that I love to have happen in games, and I'm definitely going to borrow them for use in the meantime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12167,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12167-broken-masque","user":"Broken Masque","date":". 12-05-2016, 07:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12167-broken-masque","name":"Broken Masque","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T17:01:31-08:00","id":1012873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Broken Masque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1012775-paradoxical-sidereal-thoughts?p=1012859#post1012859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I will say it's exactly the kind of weird shit that I love to have happen in games</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. That's the thing, the idea of Paradox has <i>a lot</i> of potential for fun and shenanigans of exactly the kind that Sidereals should get up to*. It's just never actually been used.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm definitely going to borrow them for use in the meantime. </div> </div> </div>Feel free <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> * by which I mean, if you look in the 1e book for what happens when Sidereals use things like Avoidance Kata, it doesn't override history or anybody's memories. People just remember the Sidereal being in the conversation <i>and also </i>leaving before the conversation began. With Ceasing to Exist Approach, the sidereal weaves themself into an entirely new millieu as though they've always been there, and everyone remembers it being so (except beings of higher essence), but they also remember that identity never existing in the first place. Both these contradictions are treated as completely unremarkable facts not worth mentioning.<br /> <br /> (1e's <i>Exalted: The Sidereals</i>, p.131 -- On Memory)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T20:29:07-08:00","id":1012958,"title":"","content":"I like the closed Charmset, hate Paradox. I'd Like @Eura 's post, save that they seem to view the closed Charmset as some sort of punishment. <br /> <br /> First off, it's not punishment, it's a limitation, and it's the kind of limitation that tends to make for more creative players, which is something I love as an ST.<br /> <br /> Second off, maybe my games haven't run long enough, but I've never had a Sidereal have enough experience to run out of Sidereal Charms (I <i>did</i> have a Solar run out of Stealth Charms back in 2e, before he had to start digging through splat-books for more ways to sneak up on people magically, but that's because there were, what, four of them in the Core? Six? I don't think Sidereals are gonna have that problem this time 'round\u2026), to the point where they had to start buying Martial Arts and Sorcery.<br /> <br /> Third, we're also going to have Evocations - from Artifacts, spells, <i>and</i> Hearthstones - and various Merits to mix into the system. You don't have to take Martial Arts if you want access to cool weird stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T03:09:30-08:00","id":1013086,"title":"","content":"I've had Sidereals run out of charms that they actually want to buy but I attribute that more to MoEP: Sidereals being a largely copy/paste that didn't take into account that 2e's growing focus on high essence (DotFA had already been announced by then and a charm was previewed in Compass West) also meant more experience.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T04:00:19-08:00","id":1013092,"title":"","content":"The problem with closed charmsets in 3e is that you can't have sidereals restricted to a big set list of things that don't exist in-setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T04:33:32-08:00","id":1013097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1012775-paradoxical-sidereal-thoughts?p=1013092#post1013092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with closed charmsets in 3e is that you can't have sidereals restricted to a big set list of things that don't exist in-setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>That assumes Sidereal Charms will/should be treated identically as the Solar Charms. I'm not so certain that will be the case. While the Solar magic both stems from and expresses itself by pushing the boundaries of human excellence, Sidereals have always drawn on the external force that is Fate to work their miracles, so it makes more sense for them to recognize particular ways of influencing it in character.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T04:42:41-08:00","id":1013098,"title":"","content":"I just want to say my current Sid has 250ish exp and I'm about to hit that point where there's no non M.A. charm I want to buy. This is with me going deep into two unfavored trees. The only big exp dump left for the build is melee and a handful of luxury charms that could be nice or never come up. Evocations will be nice and definitely help, but until we get proper guidelines on how to design them I'm weary of messing with it (as much as I want my beamklaive to have evocations).<br /> <br /> As someone whom likes to homebrew charms a lot (when I ST every single unique supernatural has a custom charm) all the limited charm set does is stifle me making unique and memorable characters. The whole &quot;your custom charm always existed&quot; just feels like a cheap way to dodge an obviously flawed rule just so we can keep saying &quot;the maidens perfectly knew what charms we needed&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm really hoping 3rd makes this argument moot and not &quot;look at all these cool things, but no seriously take martial arts&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T05:50:55-08:00","id":1013110,"title":"","content":"I liked the Setting rationale for the closed charmsets, but IMO the Sidereal charms seemed to have gaps that the All Knowing Maidens should have plugged. With larger 3e charm trees, I have faith that Sids will be able to do more and do it better. Maybe it would be nice if the Sids could create new charms, IF a Maiden signed off on it. Its a good incentive for diligent work and gives the ST a bit of wriggle room (and story opportunities).<br /> <br /> Paradox did seem a bit oppressive and Astrology looked to be a lot of work for very little gain. I'm hoping the Devs can inject some <u>fun and simplicity</u> into both areas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Long time lurker","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8781-happy-hermit","name":"Happy Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8781_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T05:52:46-08:00","id":1013111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1012775-paradoxical-sidereal-thoughts?p=1013097#post1013097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That assumes Sidereal Charms will/should be treated identically as the Solar Charms. I'm not so certain that will be the case. While the Solar magic both stems from and expresses itself by pushing the boundaries of human excellence, Sidereals have always drawn on the external force that is Fate to work their miracles, so it makes more sense for them to recognize particular ways of influencing it in character.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds more like astrology than charms though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T06:35:05-08:00","id":1013122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1012775-paradoxical-sidereal-thoughts?p=1013111#post1013111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds more like astrology than charms though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I couldn't disagree more. The section of the corebook that says Charms aren't a thing in-setting is extremely explicit about being applicable to Solar Charms, not Charms in general, and Sidereal Charms have always been Maiden-approved ways of influencing Fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T07:13:29-08:00","id":1013139,"title":"","content":"Ok, fair enough. It had been a while since I read that bit. <br /> <br /> What I'm getting here though is that Sidereals basically treat <i>every single ability</i> like a martial art. There's basically a bunch of charms that form Divine Bureaucracy Style and another set that make up Harmonious Transcendence of Dodge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T07:40:37-08:00","id":1013155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1012775-paradoxical-sidereal-thoughts?p=1013139#post1013139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, fair enough. It had been a while since I read that bit.<br /> <br /> What I'm getting here though is that Sidereals basically treat <i>every single ability</i> like a martial art. There's basically a bunch of charms that form Divine Bureaucracy Style and another set that make up Harmonious Transcendence of Dodge.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's very true, and perfectly in line with my point - Martial Arts Charms are already way more tangible in-setting than Solar Charms, by virtue of being both universal across all Exalted types and somewhat rigid means of disciplined combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T10:10:19-08:00","id":1013249,"title":"","content":"I feel like paradox might be more fun and interesting if we got a better idea of what a Fate Error really looks like. Because I don't think 2e ever really got into that and 1e didn't touch on it very much. If they can make us really understand what fate breaking down is like and then have the Paradox mechanics play into that, I think it'll be much more interesting than otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T10:52:58-08:00","id":1013269,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's a shame this aspect of bugfixing Fate was left completely blank in favor of the much more mundane &quot;make sure person X is the sole survivor of village Y&quot; and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T14:10:53-08:00","id":1013372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1012775-paradoxical-sidereal-thoughts?p=1013269#post1013269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it's a shame this aspect of bugfixing Fate was left completely blank in favor of the much more mundane &quot;make sure person X is the sole survivor of village Y&quot; and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. also would have been fun to have an idea of <i>how</i> to go about fixing these things. There were a couple indirect examples one could go off of as inspiration for glitches (stemming mostly from counterspells ruining local reality), like a blizzard in the south, a river flowing uphill and such; but <i>how</i> do sidereals deal with that? It seems like their power-set revolves more around creating and exploiting glitches than fixing them.<br /> <br /> Say a blizzard does start in Gem because someone countered Magma Kraken*. Do they just order a god to get to it? Do they do a magic dance? Do they get to knitting? do they just quarantine it off from mortals and wait for it to resolve itself?<br /> <br /> Obviously a &quot;fix causality error&quot; Charm would be boring as shit and defeat the purpose, but... yeah. How.<br /> <br /> * in this hypothetical I'm using 2e rules because I can't be arsed to come up with an other idea for what caused a reality distortion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 12-06-2016, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T02:02:56-08:00","id":1014213,"title":"","content":"The introduction of Getimians suggests fate errors are going to get more attention than they did in previous editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T06:14:45-08:00","id":1014270,"title":"","content":"As a fan of the Sidereals I'm kind of not really wedded to Paradox as &quot;If you overuse powers, then you accumulate these points and when they reach a threshold, you roll and random bad stuff happens to you&quot;. If there's any other possible balancing mechanics for what they do, totally open to that. No commitment to 'dox. It's really not-a-core-thing to me.<br /> <br /> Any kind of consequences from Paradox seem like they'd be almost always less interesting that other kind of perverse and difficult consequences a clever ST could think up to add lots of &quot;interest&quot; to the lives of Sidereal PCs.<br /> <br /> Re: fate errors and Getimians, one thing about the Getimians is that introducing them may mean that mistakes in fate can become more part of the unified (and cunning) plan of malign(?) entities who introduce or use them to achieve ends, and so a bit more useful for a general plot rather than &quot;One damn thing happening after another&quot;. That sounds a bit more interesting. Not that this shouldn't already be assumed through demons, fairies, gods, sorcerers, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T06:26:30-08:00","id":1014275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1012775-paradoxical-sidereal-thoughts?p=1014213#post1014213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The introduction of Getimians suggests fate errors are going to get more attention than they did in previous editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI'm not sure about that; Getimians themselves seem to be more about problems with Fate in the form of the actions of individuals, even if this is enhanced by giving them powers such as have been suggested.<br /> <br /> \u200bI actually recall developer quotes implying a mind to move further away from the idea of &quot;Fate errors&quot; as glitches in reality that Sidereal Charms have no actual interaction with, and focusing more on the idea of Fate as the plans of Heaven for the course of the future.<br /> <br /> \u200bI think this can still accommodate the point of giving Sidereals more weighty assignments than ensuring that the right person chokes to death on a fishbone, but still be focused more on somebody not dying when the authorities said they were supposed to because of interference, rather than somebody dying but still being alive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T11:05:50-08:00","id":1014384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1012775-paradoxical-sidereal-thoughts?p=1014275#post1014275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI'm not sure about that; Getimians themselves seem to be more about problems with Fate in the form of the actions of individuals, even if this is enhanced by giving them powers such as have been suggested.<br /> <br /> \u200bI actually recall developer quotes implying a mind to move further away from the idea of &quot;Fate errors&quot; as glitches in reality that Sidereal Charms have no actual interaction with, and focusing more on the idea of Fate as the plans of Heaven for the course of the future.<br /> <br /> \u200bI think this can still accommodate the point of giving Sidereals more weighty assignments than ensuring that the right person chokes to death on a fishbone, but still be focused more on somebody not dying when the authorities said they were supposed to because of interference, rather than somebody dying but still being alive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Well, I hope they include some other general consequences to &quot;things not going according to Heaven's plan,&quot; if they remove the whole &quot;reality breaking down&quot; aspect, because I'm gonna need more than just &quot;Chejop says I'll lose my job if I don't.&quot; <br /> <br /> Because, honestly, Heaven is a deeply broken place full of corrupt politicians so any Will of Heaven that I have to follow needs some actual reasons behind it, not just the whims of uncaring gods. Sidereals need to be able to put forth a reasonably convincing argument that they're the good guys, otherwise no-one will play them","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T11:09:30-08:00","id":1014385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1012775-paradoxical-sidereal-thoughts?p=1014384#post1014384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh. Well, I hope they include some other general consequences to &quot;things not going according to Heaven's plan,&quot; if they remove the whole &quot;reality breaking down&quot; aspect, because I'm gonna need more than just &quot;Chejop says I'll lose my job if I don't.&quot;<br /> <br /> Because, honestly, Heaven is a deeply broken place full of corrupt politicians so any Will of Heaven that I have to follow needs some actual reasons behind it, not just the whims of uncaring gods.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree. I would like heaven to be corrupt, but I don't want the answer to the corruption to be &quot;Kill all the gods because Creation will be better off without these parasitic fuckers.&quot; I want there to be a reason for Heaven's existence besides something to keep bored gods busy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T12:46:42-08:00","id":1014425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1012775-paradoxical-sidereal-thoughts?p=1014384#post1014384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh. Well, I hope they include some other general consequences to &quot;things not going according to Heaven's plan,&quot; if they remove the whole &quot;reality breaking down&quot; aspect, because I'm gonna need more than just &quot;Chejop says I'll lose my job if I don't.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably more specifically the plans of the Maidens.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt might depend on how much one assumes the Maidens make good plans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because, honestly, Heaven is a deeply broken place full of corrupt politicians</div> </div> </div> </div>Which raises the question of whether or not the corrupt gods <i>also</i> represent a deviation from the divine order.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereals need to be able to put forth a reasonably convincing argument that they're the good guys, otherwise no-one will play them</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThere are a few Scotsmen who'll play Sidereals who are less than aspirational, I'm quite sure.<br /> <br /> \u200bI think there's room for Sidereals in Third Edition to be a bit like Sidereals in The Modern Age; forced to compromise with an undesirable system because the lack of their input whatsoever would be even worse.<br /> <br /> \u200bStill, if the developers say &quot;deviation from Fate is going to be represented in character interactions rather than impersonal reality rifts&quot;, it may also depend on what the personalities they're involved with and opposed to are like. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't want the answer to the corruption to be &quot;Kill all the gods because Creation will be better off without these parasitic fuckers.&quot; I want there to be a reason for Heaven's existence besides something to keep bored gods busy.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bQuestion: do your games become really disturbing and reminiscent of Stalinist Russia any time the players come across a place ruled by corrupt human nobility? <br /> <br /> \u200bSeriously, the number of times people respond to things like this with &quot;I really desperately need to be given a reason not to play a genocidal tyrant&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200bHeh, now I'm remembering that time I had cause to rant for a while about the Great Famine, and the surrounding economic conditions of massive amounts of unemployment and scant land holdings. How, at the time, there was a perspective among some Irish and critics of the response of the British government that the Famine was a bit deliberate, out of a hope by the authorities that it would eliminate all of those useless people just taking up space and stirring up trouble on account of having so much of their land taken for cattle grazing.<br /> <br /> \u200bReally, in some games, it probably doesn't bode well for societies struggling with overpopulation. You get to the point where you've got enough wealth and magic to ensure that all economic needs can be fulfilled by a fairly small elite, and then what are you to do with the overflow?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T13:05:53-08:00","id":1014430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1012775-paradoxical-sidereal-thoughts?p=1014425#post1014425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bQuestion: do your games become really disturbing and reminiscent of Stalinist Russia any time the players come across a place ruled by corrupt human nobility?<br /> <br /> \u200bSeriously, the number of times people respond to things like this with &quot;I really desperately need to be given a reason not to play a genocidal tyrant&quot;.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Because I find in RPG games, some players are going to take the &quot;Final Solution&quot; to a problem. They are going to kill everyone, send their ghosts to Lethe, and leave no evidence behind for their family to find. Otherwise, the ST might bring that villain back for a sequel. <br /> <br /> Instead of solving the problem how their character would solve it, they want to find the &quot;correct&quot; solution. They are going to obsessively search their plans for any way the ST/GM/DM will screw* them over and &quot;fix&quot; those ways. They aren't playing to create a story; they want to <i>win</i> the game.<br /> <br /> Hell, sometimes when I've had a bad week at work, I'm one of those players.<br /> <br /> *Never mind it is the ST's job to bring conflict to the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 12-08-2016, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T13:47:47-08:00","id":1014444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1012775-paradoxical-sidereal-thoughts?p=1014430#post1014430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because I find in RPG games, some players are going to take the &quot;Final Solution&quot; to a problem. They are going to kill everyone, send their ghosts to Lethe, and leave no evidence behind for their family to find. Otherwise, the ST might bring that villain back for a sequel.<br /> <br /> Instead of solving the problem how their character would solve it, they want to find the &quot;correct&quot; solution. They are going to obsessively search their plans for any way the ST/GM/DM will screw* them over and &quot;fix&quot; those ways. They aren't playing to create a story; they want to <i>win</i> the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI really don't want the game to be written around these people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T15:36:43-08:00","id":1014488,"title":"","content":"ya I think a good rework of paradox and pattern spider bite would be a good idea - nothing lethal - and it should be something random from a table, not the same thing every time.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps something that works via how much paradox you accrue - a bit like Alchemical clararity: The more paradox you have, the more effects/punishments you get. Like a kind of miasma of reality damage you just bring with you.<br /> <br /> Like, from 0 to 3, nothing happens<br /> <br /> from 4 to 5 all your astrological curses/blessings can only last up to half as long as usual until you get down to paradox down under 3(the pattern spiders basically limiting your powers, slap on the wrist style)<br /> <br /> from 5 to 9 your damage to reality causes forces the spiders to shore up reality around you once the astrological effect that brought you up to this level is over - all astrology effects and resplendent destinies on you go away, and even the arcane fate fades, making everyone remember you...<br /> <br /> At paradox 10 you break reality - your character is forced out of fate for a 24 hour period, but only upon the end of the astrological effect that got you to paradox 10 or higher. After those 24 hours the pattern spiders have fixed your damage, and your paradox is back 0.<br /> <br /> the effects do stack here, so going from paradox 6 to 9 incurs both the 4-5 and 5-9 punishments - but again, only once the power that put you there ends. AFAIK there aren't any astrological effects that last forever.<br /> <br /> <br /> This would make paradox much less lethal and dangerous - but very annoying to anyone who uses a lot of them. Someone who uses resplendent destinies or blessings a lot, or someone who relies a lot on arcane fate to escape from things, will feel this the most. Also being out of fate for 24 hours makes it impossible to use a lot of fate related charms and whatnot.<br /> <br /> Sure, some astrological effects takes a while to fade - but that just means that you can try to time when your 'punishment' kicks in.<br /> <br /> I would of course add that you can still reduce paradox via the usual methods, plus one d2 per month of not causing any paradox at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T03:04:12-08:00","id":1014668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1012775-paradoxical-sidereal-thoughts?p=1014275#post1014275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI'm not sure about that;</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh but I am.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1012775-paradoxical-sidereal-thoughts?p=1014275#post1014275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI actually recall developer quotes implying a mind to move further away from the idea of &quot;Fate errors&quot; as glitches in reality that Sidereal Charms have no actual interaction with, and focusing more on the idea of Fate as the plans of Heaven for the course of the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't want the focus to be on anomalies like the cliff where gravity's stopped working, because-<br /> 1. It's the kind of problem that you throw magic at until it stops being a problem.<br /> 2. A major part of the desire for reality breaking down and the Sidereals having specialist charms to fix it stems from a desire for them to be indispensible in the face of the people howling for their blood over the Usurpation. That's misguided, the people doing that aren't going to stop because the mechanics conspired to make them essential. They did this with 2e Solars and some people hated them because of that shit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 12-09-2016, 06:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T04:47:06-08:00","id":1014702,"title":"","content":"Paradoxically (pardon the pun), if fate glitches of the &quot;town stuck in Groundhog Day&quot; variety are to be a part of Sidereal experience, it's absolutely imperative that Sids don't have &quot;Groundhog Day Undoing Prana&quot; anywhere in their Charmset. Charms that detect, analyze and protect against the effects of causality failures would be alright, but if such a thing is to become an adventure material, the solution has to be something for the PCs to figure out and implement by themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T05:20:30-08:00","id":1014712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1012775-paradoxical-sidereal-thoughts?p=1014668#post1014668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Oh but I am.</div> </div> </div> </div>Come on, who are you talking to here? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T06:44:51-08:00","id":1014732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1012775-paradoxical-sidereal-thoughts?p=1014668#post1014668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. A major part of the desire for reality breaking down and the Sidereals having specialist charms to fix it stems from a desire for them to be indispensible in the face of the people howling for their blood over the Usurpation. That's misguided, the people doing that aren't going to stop because the mechanics conspired to make them essential. They did this with 2e Solars and some people hated them because of that shit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I just wanna play Demon: The Descent, Exalted Edition :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}